<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<ModMetaData>
	<name>The Dead Man's Switch - Taktikmagier</name>
	<modIconPath IgnoreIfNoMatchingField="True">UI/NaraLogo</modIconPath>
  	<author>AobaKuma ,Bill Doors, KV4EX</author>
	<!--
		1.7 only, same as DMS 2. DMS 2's LoadFolders.xml has no 1.6 node, so on 1.6 the core mod
		loads nothing and this mod's defs (which inherit DMS bases) would have nothing to stand on.

		Royalty is required: magier spells are vanilla psycasts, and Psycast.Activate refuses to run
		without Royalty (ModLister.CheckRoyalty). Neural heat also needs Royalty's PsychicEntropy hediff.
	-->
	<supportedVersions>
		<li>1.7</li>
	</supportedVersions>
	<packageId>Aoba.DeadManSwitch.Taktikmagier</packageId>
	<modDependencies>
		<li>
			<packageId>brrainz.harmony</packageId>
			<displayName>Harmony</displayName>
			<steamWorkshopUrl>https://steamcommunity.com/workshop/filedetails/?id=2009463077</steamWorkshopUrl>
			<downloadUrl>https://github.com/pardeike/HarmonyRimWorld/releases/latest</downloadUrl>
		</li>
		<li>
			<packageId>ludeon.rimworld.royalty</packageId>
			<displayName>Royalty</displayName>
		</li>
		<li>
			<packageId>Aoba.DeadManSwitch.Core</packageId>
			<steamWorkshopUrl>https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3121742525</steamWorkshopUrl>
			<displayName>Dead Man Switch</displayName>
		</li>
	</modDependencies>
	<loadAfter>
		<li>brrainz.harmony</li>
		<li>AOBA.Framework</li>
		<li>Aoba.DeadManSwitch.Core</li>
		<li>vanillaexpanded.achievements</li>
  	</loadAfter>
	<description>Millennia earlier, as the threat of archotech war machines, pirates and awry bio-organic weapons arise. Nara Industries initiated a project of semi-automated war-machines, which aimed at creating a legion of war-machines with low technology and maintenance requirements to aid humans in all galaxy to the war against all those threats.</description>
</ModMetaData>
